{"results":[{"url":"https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/nicco-vanashri-heights/324237/project","title":"Nicco Vanashri Heights, Borivali West, Mumbai - Price Starts from ₹2.59 Cr Onwards | 2, 3 BHK Flats Available","raw_content":"![Squareyards Logo](/assets/images/squareyards.png?aio=w-82;h-32;crop;)\n![New India Construction Company developer logo](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/developerlogo/new-india-construction-company-10360.jpg?aio=w-128;h-128;crop;)\n\n# Nicco Vanashri Heights Borivali West, Mumbai\n\n![Nicco Vanashri Heights Cover Image](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-project-project-large-image1-6125.jpg?aio=w-725;h-350;crop;)\n![Nicco Vanashri Heights Floor Plans](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-project-floor-plans1-7132.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n![Nicco Vanashri Heights Floor Plans](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-project-floor-plans5-5815.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n![Nicco Vanashri Heights Video](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/tn-projectflagship/tn-nicco-vanashri-heights-project-flagship.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n\n**₹2.59 Cr - 5.62 Cr**\n\n₹31,750 Per Sq. Ft.\n\n## Why you should consider Nicco Vanashri Heights?\n\n## Nicco Vanashri Heights Price List, Price Trends and Market Insights\n\n### Price List\n\nView the latest price list for Nicco Vanashri Heights.\n\n| Unit Type (Carpet) | Price\\* | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 BHK Apartment  732 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 2.59 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 2 BHK Apartment  750 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 2.65 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  1035 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 3.66 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  1591 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 5.62 Cr** | Check Availability |\n\n\\*Prices are indicative and subject to applicable charges and project terms.\n\n### Price Trends\n\nNicco Vanashri Heights's average asking price is stable quarter-on-quarter, compared with Borivali West.\n\nSep 2025 — Jun 2026\n\n| Quarter | Nicco Vanashri Heights | Borivali West |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Jun 2026 | 31750 | 30900 |\n| Mar 2026 | 31700 | 31300 |\n| Dec 2025 | 30900 | 30300 |\n| Sep 2025 | 30900 | 30350 |\n\n### Comparable Projects\n\nNicco Vanashri Heights avg. price is ₹ 31.8 K/Sq.Ft. compared to Borivali West at ₹ 30.9 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Project | Avg. ₹/sq ft |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Godrej Reserve Kandivali](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/godrej-reserve-kandivali/243614/project \"Godrej Reserve Kandivali\") | ₹ 42,450 |\n| [Chandak Greenairy](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/chandak-greenairy/152458/project \"Chandak Greenairy\") | ₹ 37,100 |\n| Current Project **Nicco Vanashri Heights** | ₹ 31,750 |\n| Borivali West | ₹ 30,900 |\n| [Mahindra Vista](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/mahindra-vista/243232/project \"Mahindra Vista\") | ₹ 30,700 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Borivali West ranges from ₹ 22.1 K to ₹ 74.4 K with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In Nicco Vanashri Heights | In Borivali West |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 32.7 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 45.5 K |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 74.4 K |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for Nicco Vanashri Heights.\n\n#### MMRDA Plans Two New Ring Roads to Ease Mumbai Traffic\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) is planning two additional ring routes, expanding its proposed network from seven to nine. These new corridors will cover approximately 307 km and will connect existing roads and planned projects across Mumbai, Thane, and Navi Mumbai.\n\n#### Thane Infrastructure and Development Updates\n\nThe Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel project saw the launch of TBM Arjuna on August 13, 2026, aiming to reduce travel time between Thane and Borivali to approximately 15 minutes. Amazon Data Services is developing a large data center in Ambernath, with an estimated construction cost of ₹3,500 crore, to be ready by 2029\n\n#### Mumbai Boosts Connectivity with Santacruz - Chembur link road Phase 2 & Chembur Metro Station\n\nCM Devendra Fadnavis inaugurated Phase 2 of the Santacruz-Chembur Link Road (SCLR) & the Chembur Metro Station under Metro Line 2B,The SCLR Phase 2 is expected to strengthen the road network between Mumbai's western and eastern suburbs, improving east-west connectivity.\n\n#### Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel Project: Traffic Diversions Announced in Kasarvadavali\n\nTemporary traffic diversions have been implemented in Kasarvadavali for the ongoing work on the ambitious Thane-Borivali twin tunnel project by the Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA). Certain routes will be closed from July 6 to August 5, 2026, to facilitate construction.\n\n#### Mumbai Monorail Services to Resume After Nine-Month Hiatus\n\nMumbai's monorail services are set to resume soon after a nine-month suspension, following approval from the Maharashtra government for safety improvements and fare revisions. MMRDA has proposed increased ticket prices. The monorail, which previously carried around 18,000 passengers daily, will offer improved services after safety upgrades.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for Nicco Vanashri Heights moved from ₹ 31,700/sqft to ₹ 31,750/sqft, reflecting a 0.16% rise.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\n## Nicco Vanashri Heights Floor Plans\n\n![Floor plan of 2 BHK 732 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Nicco Vanashri Heights, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/unit-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-apartment-2-bhk-732sqft-20254117114158-3d-3401.jpg?aio=w-392;h-392;crop;)\n\nPrice:₹ 2.59 Cr\n\n![Floor plan of 2 BHK 750 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Nicco Vanashri Heights, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/unit-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-apartment-2-bhk-826sqft-20254417114424-3d-1986.jpg?aio=w-392;h-392;crop;)\n\nPrice:₹ 2.65 Cr\n\n![Floor plan of 3 BHK 1035 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Nicco Vanashri Heights, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/unit-image/nicco-vanashri-heights-apartment-3-bhk-1036sqft-20254117114139-3d-9155.jpg?aio=w-392;h-392;crop;)\n\nPrice:₹ 3.66 Cr\n\n![Floor plan of 3 BHK 1591 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Nicco Vanashri Heights, Mumbai